# Routes Module (`backend/src/routes`)

## Purpose

This module defines the API routes for the application using Express Routers. Each file typically corresponds to a major feature or entity and maps HTTP methods and URL paths to specific controller functions.

## Main Components

- `auth.routes.ts`: Defines routes for authentication (e.g., `/login`, `/register`).
- `bim.routes.ts`: Defines routes for BIM functionalities.
- `file.routes.ts`: Defines routes for file operations.
- `material.routes.ts`: Defines routes for material management.
- `project.routes.ts`: Defines routes for project CRUD and other project-related actions.
- `role.routes.ts`: Defines routes for role and permission management.
- `site-visit.routes.ts`: Defines routes for site visit functionalities.
- `siteVisitBox.routes.ts`: Defines routes for site visit box configurations.
- `user.routes.ts`: Defines routes for user management (e.g., CRUD operations on users).

## Key Functionalities (to be detailed for each route file)

- Creating instances of `express.Router()`.
- Defining route handlers for various HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH).
- Mapping URL paths (e.g., `/api/users/:id`) to controller functions.
- Applying route-specific middleware (e.g., `auth.middleware.ts`, `admin.middleware.ts`, validation middleware).

## Interactions (to be detailed for each route file)

- How each router is imported and mounted onto the main Express app in `server.ts` or `index.ts` (e.g., `app.use('/api/auth', authRouter)`).
- Which controller functions (from the `controllers` module) are invoked by each route definition.
- Which middlewares (from `middlewares` or `common/middleware` modules) are applied to specific routes or the entire router.
